    {
      "@id": "urn:oslo-toolchain:866edcf86c9a4fa8b535a1b6d2602ed0295ba61e058b9484988522dc21b02ab8",
      "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty",
      "apDefinition": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Kenmerk van het Verkeersobject dat geobserveerd wordt."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Characteristic of the TrafficObject being observed."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Characteristic of the TrafficObject being observed."
        }
      ],
      "apLabel": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "geobserveerdKenmerk"
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "observedFeature"
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "observedFeature"
        }
      ],
      "apUsageNote": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "CONSTRAINT: Het geobserveerdKenmerk moet werkelijk een kenmerk zijn van het geobserveerdObject of van een (onder)deel ervan. Soms is de procedure waarmee de waarden vh kenmerk worden bekomen indirect, ttz men meet om praktische reden een ander kenmerk dat een proxy is voor het kenmerk dat men werkelijk wil observeren. Bv om de Verkeersintensiteit op een Wegsegment te bepalen telt men individuele doorkomsten van Voertuigen in een Verkeersmeetpunt."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "CONSTRAINT: The observedFeature must actually be a feature of the observedObject or of a (sub)part of it. Sometimes the procedure by which the values of the feature are obtained is indirect, i.e. for practical reasons one measures another feature that is a proxy for the feature that one really wants to observe. For example, to determine the TrafficIntensity on a RoadSegment, individual passes by Vehicles at a Traffic MeasuringPoint are counted."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "CONSTRAINT: The observedFeature must actually be a feature of the observedObject or of a (sub)part of it. Sometimes the procedure by which the values of the feature are obtained is indirect, i.e. for practical reasons one measures another feature that is a proxy for the feature that one really wants to observe. For example, to determine the TrafficIntensity on a RoadSegment, individual passes by Vehicles at a Traffic MeasuringPoint are counted."
        }
      ],
      "assignedURI": "https://data.vlaanderen.be/ns/verkeersmetingen#geobserveerdKenmerk",
      "diagramLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "geobserveerdKenmerk"
        }
      ],
