          "@value": "observedObject"
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "observedObject"
        }
      ],
      "apUsageNote": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Dat kan het Verkeersdomeinobject zelf zijn of een proxy ervan, ttz een Verkeersbemonsteringsobject. OPMERKING: In dat laatste geval weet men soms pas na het observeren welk real-world Object men juist geobserveerd heeft. bvb in een Verkeersmeetpunt weet men niet op voorhand welke de Voertuigen zullen zijn waarvan men de snelheid zal vaststellen."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "This can be the TrafficDomainObject itself or a proxy of it, i.e. a TrafficSamplingObject. NOTE: In the latter case, one sometimes only knows after observing which real-world Object one has observed. At a Traffic Measurement Point, one does not know in advance of which Vehicles exactly one will determine the speed."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "This can be the TrafficDomainObject itself or a proxy of it, i.e. a TrafficSamplingObject. NOTE: In the latter case, one sometimes only knows after observing which real-world Object one has observed. At a Traffic Measurement Point, one does not know in advance of which Vehicles exactly one will determine the speed."
        }
